        <h2 class="section-title">FAST SUBSTATION BUSBAR PROTECTION WITH IEC 61850 AND GOOSE</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
        <h2 class="section-title">Fast substation busbar protection with IEC 61850 and GOOSE</h2>
        <p class="subtitle">Falu Elnät AB applies new power system protection and automation technology</p>
    </div>

    <div class="two-column">
        <div class="column">
            <p class="body-text">
                <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span>, a subsidiary of <span data-field="company.parent_name">{{ company.parent_name }}</span> and <span data-field="company.other_parent">{{ company.other_parent }}</span>, is a municipality-owned transmission and distribution company located in the municipality of <span data-field="location.municipality">{{ location.municipality }}</span>, approximately <span data-field="location.distance">{{ location.distance }}</span> north of Stockholm, the capital of Sweden. In <span data-field="year">{{ year }}</span>, <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span> and <span data-field="company.other_parent">{{ company.other_parent }}</span> signed a three-year frame agreement including native IEC 61850 standards.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span> aims to strengthen its role in the energy transition by implementing the latest technology in the field of power system protection and control for fast and selective protection and future proof solutions.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span> distributes electricity to approximately <span data-field="customer_count">{{ customer_count }}</span> customers in the municipality of <span data-field="location.municipality">{{ location.municipality }}</span>. The parent company, <span data-field="company.parent_name">{{ company.parent_name }}</span>, is apart from being the owner of <span data-field="company.other_parent">{{ company.other_parent }}</span>, the largest shareholder of <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span>, a collaboration of nine energy companies in the region. Due to the deregulation of the electricity market in the mid 90's the power generation and distribution were separated into two different companies within <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span>. The transmission and distribution network of <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span> comprises 23 substations, over <span data-field="asset_count">{{ asset_count }}</span> of overhead power lines and more than <span data-field="asset_count_2">{{ asset_count_2 }}</span> km of underground cables for the supply of approximately <span data-field="power_capacity">{{ power_capacity }}</span> GWh of electricity to its customers. The company has strategically invested in underground cables in order to create a weather-proof network and to increase the reliability of the power supply. Furthermore, by investing in new protection and control equipment and utilizing the thorough knowledge of the personnel, <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span> aims at serving the customers better even in network disturbance situations.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <p class="body-text">
                The Linghed substation, operated by <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span>, supplies power from the grid and a wind power park to the local community.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="image-container">
