<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="width: 45%;">
            <h3 class="section-title">Christier Johansson</h3>
            <p class="body-text">Operations Manager of <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span></p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 50%; text-align: center;">
            <!-- Placeholder for the portrait photo -->
            <img src="placeholder_portrait_photo.png" alt="Portrait" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="two-column" style="margin-top: 30px;">
        <div class="column">
            <h3 class="section-title">Renewed substation in Linghed to increase the reliability of the power distribution</h3>
            <p class="body-text">
                The <span data-field="substation.name">{{ substation.name }}</span> in Linghed, situated some <span data-field="distance">{{ distance }}</span> km north of the city centre of <span data-field="location.municipality">{{ location.municipality }}</span>, was built in <span data-field="year">{{ year }}</span> and equipped with <span data-field="equipment_type">{{ equipment_type }}</span>. The substation is connected to Fortum's grid and it is fed from two power transformers. The three winding (T2) 55/22 kV transformer rated 16/10 MVA was built in <span data-field="year">{{ year }}</span> and the other winding (T1) 55/11.5 kV rated 10 MVA is currently used for backup purposes. The two transformers feed the local 11 kV distribution network and connects to the 22 kV line of the wind power park at <span data-field="location.park_name">{{ location.park_name }}</span>. For protection of the new power transformer, Protection IEC Falu Elnät aims at increasing the reliability of the power supply by using protection solutions with two power transformers, a main transformer and a backup transformer. Two power transformers allow undeniable maintenance flexibility and security of supply. The transformer maintenance planning can thereby be based on the actual need instead of on a fixed available time from a network perspective. "Having two power transformers is a strong benefit seen from the maintenance point of view. We don't have two transformers through out the network but nevertheless in many substations. We have a number of substations with a single power transformer and the problem is that the tap-changer revisions must be done during a low-load summer period.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                Now we can do the maintenance work at any time because now the network can be operated with two power production. "Says <span data-field="person.name">{{ person.name }}</span>, Operations Manager of <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span>.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <h3 class="section-title">Protection and Control REF615 IEDs (Intelligent Electronic Device)</h3>
            <p class="body-text">
                <span data-field="person.name">{{ person.name }}</span>, Operations Manager, explains that ABB offers a complete solution for protection and control equipment that was able to meet the requirements of the substation. The protection and control IEDs are designed to be highly reliable, redundant, and interoperable. The IEDs are based on the IEC 61850 standard, which allows for seamless communication between all components of the substation. The IEDs are configured for one configuration tool for all of the IEDs.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                <span data-field="person.name">{{ person.name }}</span>, Operations Manager of <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span>, states that the solution has allowed them to increase the reliability of the power supply, which is crucial for the local community.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="two-column" style="margin-top: 30px;">
        <div class="column">
            <h3 class="section-title">Life cycle and asset management</h3>
            <p class="body-text">
                The renewal of the Linghed substation included the implementation of a modern substation automation system including CBS but to exchange the existing protection relays. Thanks to the built-in CB condition monitoring of the REF615 devices the life-cycle of the current CBS of a substation can be prolonged for increased cost-efficiency. This will extend the life-cycle of the substation through the utilization of the whole substation's life-cycle of the switchgear and its CBS.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                The decision meant that the investment costs were optimized. The protection system was modernized to ensure a fast and selective operation in fault situations while minimizing incorrect and unwanted tripping of circuit breakers. "At the moment we have a very high exchange parameter and we have 20 years, so it is about time to exchange the protection system," says <span data-field="person.name">{{ person.name }}</span>, Operations Manager.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                During the renewal of the substation a new communication network (LAN) was installed for the IEC 61850 communication including GOOSE. During the offer of the substation the remote communication system was renewed.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <h3 class="section-title">New implementation of traditional protection</h3>
            <p class="body-text">
                <span data-field="person.name">{{ person.name }}</span> states that the advantage of the IEC 61850 standard and its GOOSE service. The GOOSE service of IEC 61850 can be used for implementing fast protection schemes, which is a significant advantage over the conventional hard-wired blocking signal paths between the switchgear cubicles are replaced with a substation-wide Ethernet LAN.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                The supervision function of the GOOSE service generates an alert, should the message not get through, allowing appropriate repair measures to be taken immediately. This is a great advantage, as it allows for immediate corrective measures to be taken based on blockings has been broken nobody knows what is wrong. The GOOSE service allows for immediate corrective measures to be taken.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                The substation in Linghed is located just <span data-field="distance">{{ distance }}</span> km SW of the new wind power park at <span data-field="location.park_name">{{ location.park_name }}</span>. The substation is connected to the Linghed substation with a 22 kV line. The wind turbines are owned by <span data-field="owner.name">{{ owner.name }}</span> and are strategically in line with the energy transition in the region. <span data-field="company.name">{{ company.name }}</span> has invested in hydro- and biomass power plants, thus aiming at a reduction of the CO2 emissions by 145 000 tons a year.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div class="two-column">
        <div class="column">
            <h3 class="section-title">Fast and reliable busbar protection with GOOSE</h3>
            <p class="body-text">
                By transferring GOOSE messages between IEDs, the protection system can achieve a very fast and reliable protection. The blocking signals can be sent directly from the IEDs to the switchgear cubicles, which is a significant advantage over the conventional hard-wired blocking signal paths. This additional delay must be taken into account when the total operating time of the protection is determined.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                By means of the new technology the traditional protection system can be replaced by a modern and flexible system. The requirement has been an operating time of 150 ms. This setting has been used in the past. I have now done some testing showing that when using GOOSE even 40 ms is possible. This is a significant improvement in terms of operating time of the busbar protection will be sped up correspondingly.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                The operational reliability of a blocking-based busbar protection scheme with GOOSE messaging is significantly enhanced compared to the traditional scheme of the GOOSE service. Further, the blocking principle is not dependent on the physical wiring between the switchgear cubicles, which will not render the protection system inoperable, but may allow unwanted tripping.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <h3 class="section-title">Towards the future with IEC 61850</h3>
            <p class="body-text">
                Over the coming years Falu Elnät will continue renewing the protection and control devices of other substations in the transmission and distribution network. All substations will be equipped with IEC 61850 compliant devices thus putting the company at the forefront of the energy transition. During the renewal of the Linghed substation, the company has gained experience in the implementation of IEC 61850 and GOOSE.
            </p>
            <p class="body-text">
                The renewal of the Linghed substation will continue during 2011 with the replacement of the protection and automation devices of the two-winding power transformer with an ABB Transformer Protection and Control Device REF615. It is a big step for the company to adopt this modern technology to a completely new one. It is a matter of optimizing the protection system and to ensure a fast and selective operation in fault situations while minimizing incorrect and unwanted tripping of circuit breakers. "At the moment we have a very high exchange parameter and we have 20 years, so it is about time to exchange the protection system," says <span data-field="person.name">{{ person.name }}</span>, Operations Manager.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

